{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Prove the ADR 0118 safety gate before this repository enables `compact.snapshot_alpha`. This ticket is evidence-only: it runs an independent two-clone proof and records the commands/results on the ticket; it does not modify repository code or `rebar.toml`.\n\n## Scope\n- Use an independent throwaway Git repository and clone pair under `/Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/redstart-proof-repo`, never the live `.tickets-tracker` store.\n- Configure `compact.snapshot_alpha` only inside the throwaway clones.\n- Create divergent adaptive fold points in two clones, merge/fetch the ticket history, replay compiled ticket state, and run fsck/rebuild checks.\n- Measure this repository's live ticket-size distribution read-only and recommend an alpha with storage/replay tradeoffs.\n- Do not enable `compact.snapshot_alpha` for this repository; that is reserved for `equitable-upper-hammerkop` and is gated on this proof having zero divergence.\n\n## Proof command\nRun the artifact script:\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python /Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/redstart-proof.py`\n\nThe script executes this concrete proof sequence:\n1. Create a throwaway bare Git remote and clone `clone-a`.\n2. Seed a minimal project with `rebar.toml` containing `[compact] snapshot_alpha = 0.05`, `threshold = 9999`, `COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS = 0`, and normal sync to `origin`.\n3. Run `rebar init`, create one task, add large base comments with sync disabled, and run `REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD=0 REBAR_COMPACT_SNAPSHOT_ALPHA=0.05 rebar compact-all --limit=1` to create the first snapshot through the same sweep selection path that owns `snapshot_alpha`.\n4. Clone `clone-b` from the same remote and materialize the same ticket store.\n5. In clone A add four large A-tail comments with sync disabled and run `REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD=9999 REBAR_COMPACT_SNAPSHOT_ALPHA=0.05 rebar compact-all --limit=1`; because the foldable count is below 9999 and a snapshot already exists, only the byte alpha arm can select the ticket and create the A fold point.\n6. In clone B add two larger B-tail comments with sync disabled and run the same high-threshold `compact-all --limit=1`, creating a different B fold point through the byte alpha arm.\n7. Publish A, merge A into B, publish B, merge the combined `origin/tickets` branch back to A, run `rebar fsck` in both clones, and compare normalized `rebar show` output.\n8. Fail nonzero if the final compiled states differ.\n\n## Calibration command\nRun the read-only live-store measurement artifact:\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python /Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/redstart-calibration.py`\n\nThe calibration script walks `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker`, measures active SNAPSHOT bytes and active non-snapshot source bytes per ticket, reports percentiles, and compares alpha candidates 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, and 2.0 by estimated future replay-tail bytes and retained snapshot amplification.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Independent two-clone reconvergence proof is run in a non-live throwaway repository and the exact commands/results are recorded in ticket comments.\n- [ ] Divergent adaptive fold points converge after fetch/merge/replay/fsck without data loss or state divergence.\n- [ ] Calibration evidence records this repository's ticket-size distribution and recommends an alpha with storage and replay-cost tradeoffs.\n- [ ] `compact.snapshot_alpha` remains absent from this repository's `rebar.toml` in this ticket, proven with `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c \"from pathlib import Path; raise SystemExit('snapshot_alpha present' if 'snapshot_alpha' in Path('rebar.toml').read_text() else 0)\"`.\n- [ ] No repository files are changed by this evidence-only proof.\n\n## Verification\n- [ ] Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python /Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/redstart-proof.py`.\n- [ ] Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python /Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/redstart-calibration.py` and record its output on the ticket.\n- [ ] Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c \"from pathlib import Path; raise SystemExit('snapshot_alpha present' if 'snapshot_alpha' in Path('rebar.toml').read_text() else 0)\"`.\n- [ ] Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" git diff --exit-code` to confirm no repository file changes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789018774016539001,"uuid":"e9ace748-7594-4d40-a946-1310b9127ee7"}